%e A398464    3  | 1   2   2   1
%e A398464    4  | 1   2   5   7   6   3
%e A398464    5  | 1   2   8  14  23  29  25  15   3
%e A398464    6  | 1   2  10  21  45  81 113 142 140 105  51  9
%e A398464    ...
%e A398464 The sum of each row is n! (A000142), since each row gives the distribution of all n! permutations according to the number of comparisons required by binary insertion sort. For example, for n=3, there are six possible permutations. Of these, exactly one permutation, namely <3,1,2>, requires the maximum of three comparisons. The other permutations require two comparisons (<1,3,2> and <3,2,1>), one comparison (<2,3,1> and <2,1,3>), or zero comparisons (<1,2,3>).
%t A398464 p[n_, x_] := Product[1+(2^Ceiling[Log2[i]]-i)x^(Ceiling[Log2[i]]-1)+(2i-2^Ceiling[Log2[i]]-1)x^Ceiling[Log2[i]], {i,2,n}]; Table[CoefficientList[Expand@p[n,"x"],"x"], {n,0,8}] // Flatten
%Y A398464 Row sums give A000142.
%Y A398464 Column k=0 give A000012.
%Y A398464 Right elements of the triangle give A375959.
%Y A398464 For n>0, lengths of rows are in A083652 and A296349.
%Y A398464 Cf. A395685, A001855, A029837, A006257.
